commit 9a26e5d4e53870bb13a3f9eaaba6d5cce1ecb907
Author: Hui Shi <kalinshi@tencent.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 27 18:16:08 2026 +0800

    [Feature] Transposed (ETAP) sparse prefill kernel for small head counts on SM90
    
    Small head counts (h_q = 8 / 16 / 32) cannot fill the 64-row M dimension of
    WGMMA, so the existing small-heads kernel pads them and runs on mma.sync. This
    adds a transposed-attention kernel that puts keys on M and heads on N instead:
    
      S^T [64 keys x H] = K Q^T,    O^T [512 x H] = V^T P^T
    
    so the head count needs no padding and both GEMMs run on WGMMA. The CTA layout
    follows the 64-head kernel: a persistent CTA walks over queries, two math
    warpgroups and one producer warpgroup share two KV buffers. Each math
    warpgroup runs its own online softmax over its blocks (even / odd) into a full
    O^T and the two partial softmax states are merged in the epilogue, so the
    warpgroups never wait for each other inside the loop; the producer gathers the
    next query's Q and KV blocks while the epilogue of the previous one runs.
    
    Column-max and column-sum reductions run across the 4 warps of a warpgroup
    (log2 domain for the max, natural domain sums kept per thread until the
    epilogue), and the epilogue transposes O^T to the [head][dim] layout through
    the KV buffers before writing it through the output strides, so head-slice
    outputs stay supported.
    
    d_qk = 512 and 576 are both supported: KV rows are split into 64-element tiles
    and the trailing RoPE tile of d_qk = 576 only enters the QK GEMM, since V is
    the first 512 dims of every row. d_v stays 512, as for every other prefill
    path. The 64 / 128 head paths are unchanged.
    
    The new kernel is the default. USE_MMA_FOR_SMALL_N_HEAD=1 selects the previous
    mma.sync kernel for comparison; it is read per call, so the two can be
    benchmarked against each other in one process.
    
    On H20, bf16, 8192 tokens, against the previous small-heads kernel at topk 640:
    2.10x / 1.64x / 1.78x at h_q = 8 / 16 / 32 with d_qk = 512, and 2.29x / 1.80x /
    1.79x with d_qk = 576.
    
    Tests: the existing small-heads cases now run on this kernel for both head
    dims, plus a pairwise check against the 64-head kernel on zero-padded Q
    (topk 64 / 192 / 640 / 2048, more queries than SMs, mixed and empty lengths),
    a repeat-determinism check, and a check that the mma switch agrees with the
    default and that USE_MMA_FOR_SMALL_N_HEAD=0 keeps it.
    
    Reference: "FlashMLA-ETAP: Efficient Transpose Attention Pipeline for
    Accelerating MLA Inference on NVIDIA H20 GPUs", arXiv:2506.01969,
    https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.01969
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

